WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.870
Each autumn, for nine nights,
millions of Hindus honour Durga,

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.710
a warrior goddess.

3
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:12.170
Earlier in the year, at a full moon, a
sister ties a thread on her brother's wrist.

4
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.860
One is a goddess armed for battle.

5
00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.900
The other is a few strands
of coloured cotton.

6
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.640
They look like opposites.

7
00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:23.480
So what links a warrior
goddess and a simple thread?

8
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:27.220
In this mission, you'll follow the
stories behind these festivals,

9
00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.390
and see how Hindus keep them.

10
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.620
Then you'll weigh up how much
festivals matter to Hindus today.

11
00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:38.030
Your mission: find out what links
the warrior goddess and the thread.
